MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The SCM RPC varargs kill (ccontext == 0x10, ml218..ml320): sechost's checker
stub reads its delay-import aux slot from the module's JIT-POOL COPY, but
LdrResolveDelayLoadedAPI only ever wrote the PE-side .data — the pool slot
stayed at the unresolved lazy thunk forever, so every call took the x64 lazy
path through emulation with a NATIVE caller frame, losing the x4/x5 varargs
descriptor (NdrClientCall2's context handle became x5 = the stack-args SIZE).

1. LdrResolveDelayLoadedAPI: after the PE-side store, translate the slot
   through xlate_ios_jit and write the pool-side copy too (ml317, POOL-SYNCED
   6/6 in ml318).
2. ios_eager_delay_resolve(): resolve delay imports for ALREADY-LOADED targets
   at LdrLoadDll completion, before any call goes through them — the first
   call through a lazy slot is unsalvageable and Steam does not retry a failed
   OpenSCManagerW (ml318 exit 1). Hard-gated after ml319 (STATUS_STACK_OVERFLOW
   at 284 calls): imports_fixup_done + EC dispatchers installed + reentrancy
   flag; failures absorbed by a NULL-returning dllhook.

ml320: ndr-shift 0 (first time since ml218), sechost->rpcrt4 resolved=9
failed=0, updater GUI back, cef_log reached, deepest run ever (48,402 calls).

Also: signal_arm64ec.c KiUserExceptionDispatcher NULL-slot fall-through and
arm64ec init-phase splits from the same investigation line.

